 major source of bias in randomized controlled trials of treatments for schizophrenia</article-title><source>British Journal of Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year><volume>176</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10755072</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1192/bjp.176.3.249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adams</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Awad</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rathbone</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Thornley</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chlorpromazine versus placebo for schizophrenia</article-title><source>Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews</source><year>2007</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>CD000284</fpage><comment></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17443500</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><article-title>WHO Handbook for Reporting Results of Cancer Treatment</article-title><source>WHO Offset publication No 48</source><year>1979</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoogstraten</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Staquet</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Winkler</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reporting results of cancer treatment</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1981</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7459811</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1097-0142(19810101)47:1&#x0003c;207::AID-CNCR2820470134&